@{
  ViewData["Title"] = "Website Care Plans & Monthly Retainers | Clint McMahon";
  ViewData["Description"] = "Monthly care plans for WordPress, Umbraco, Shopify and custom .NET sites. Guaranteed response time, proactive updates, monitoring and a monthly block of hours.";
}

<div class="services page">
  <section class="container py-5">
    <header class="mb-5 text-center">
      <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold">Website Care Plans</h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted">Guaranteed access instead of hoping I have capacity when something breaks</p>
    </header>

    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
        <p class="lead">Most site owners only call a developer when something is already wrong. By then you are waiting on someone else's schedule.</p>
        <p>A care plan changes the arrangement. Instead of calling when something breaks and waiting for me to have room, a fixed monthly block buys you priority and a defined response time. Updates get applied before they turn into incidents, and when you do need something you are already at the front of the line.</p>
        <p>You are buying guaranteed access. The maintenance is what keeps the quiet months quiet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">What's Included</h3>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Defined response time.</strong> A committed window for getting back to you, in writing, rather than a best effort.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>A monthly block of hours.</strong> Use it for features, content changes, integration work or firefighting. Whatever you need that month.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Platform and plugin updates.</strong> WordPress core and plugins, Umbraco minor versions, Shopify app updates and .NET dependency patching.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Security patching.</strong> Applied on a schedule rather than after a disclosure.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Uptime and error monitoring.</strong> So you hear about problems from me and not from a customer.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Backups, verified.</strong> Backups that are tested by restoring them.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Performance checks.</strong> Periodic review of load times and Core Web Vitals, with fixes inside your hour block.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Integration monitoring.</strong> Payment, email, CRM and fulfillment integrations break when vendors change APIs. Watching for that is part of the plan.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">How It Works</h3>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Month to month.</strong> No annual lock-in. If it is not earning its keep, cancel it.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Hours do not roll over.</strong> The block is reserved capacity, which is what makes the response time possible.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Bigger work is quoted separately.</strong> A redesign or a platform migration is a project, not a care plan. The plan covers the ongoing part.</li>
          <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Billed monthly.</strong> One predictable line item instead of unpredictable invoices after every incident.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-md-8 offset-md-2">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">Platforms I Support</h3>
        <p>WordPress and WordPress Multisite, Umbraco, Shopify, and custom .NET applications on Azure or AWS. If I built it, I can maintain it. If someone else built it, I will look at it first and tell you whether taking it on makes sense.</p>
        <p>Related: <a href="/services/wordpress-hosting">WordPress hosting and development</a>, <a href="/services/umbraco-consulting">Umbraco consulting</a>, and <a href="/services/shopify-ecommerce-development">Shopify development</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="fw-bold">Want predictable support instead of emergencies?</h2>
      <p>Tell me what you are running and how often it needs attention. I will tell you what size plan fits.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg mt-3">Ask About a Care Plan</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
